**Flagging duplicate slug collisions**
codex
I’ve confirmed reproducible correctness issues in the new slug behavior (duplicate plan slugs are allowed and slug-based plan lookup becomes ambiguous). I’m writing a `REQUEST_CHANGES` review with inline comments and posting it now.
exec
/usr/bin/bash -lc "cat > /tmp/codex-pr-342-review.md <<'EOF'
MUST-FIX
1. Auto-generated plan slugs are not checked for uniqueness in "'`plan add`.
Evidence: creating two plans with the same title creates two `plan-my-feature` slugs; `plan get @plan-my-feature` resolves only one plan and the other is unreachable by slug.
Location: `src/cli/commands/plan.ts:126`

2. Auto-generated plan slugs are not checked for uniqueness in `plan import`.
Evidence: imports with the same plan title generate the same `plan-<title>` slug and create ambiguous plan refs.
Location: `src/cli/commands/plan-import.ts:165`

3. Manual slug collision checks do not include existing plans.
`buildIndexes(ctx)` indexes tasks/specs only, so `plan add --slug <existing-plan-slug>` and `plan set --slug <existing-plan-slug>` are still allowed.
Evidence: two plans can be created with `--slug custom-slug`; `plan get @custom-slug` returns only one.
Locations: `src/cli/commands/plan.ts:130`, `src/cli/commands/plan.ts:283`

SHOULD-FIX
1. Add regression tests for duplicate plan slug prevention across:
- `plan add` with same title twice
- `plan import` with same title twice
- `plan add/set --slug` colliding with an existing plan slug

SUGGESTION
1. Reuse a single slug-uniqueness helper (for tasks/specs/plans) instead of ad-hoc `refIndex.resolve()` checks, so duplicate-slug semantics are consistent for normal and already-duplicate states.

Note: PR body has no `Task: @...` trailer, so AC-by-spec coverage checks were skipped per instructions.
EOF

